---
import Section from './Section.astro';
// A faithfully rendered coach exchange in v4's plain voice. The visible data
// lookup (query_metric) stays — it's the mechanism no competitor shows — but the
// research-note citation tags are gone (owner: stop proving it academically).
---

<Section id="coach" tone="sunk" labelledby="coach-h">
  <h2 id="coach-h" class="rise mt-4 max-w-2xl text-[clamp(1.9rem,4vw,3rem)]">
    Ask it anything. It looks up your real numbers before it answers.
  </h2>
  <p class="lede rise mt-6 max-w-2xl">
    A coach that isn’t checked can say whatever sounds nice. Ours pulls your actual numbers first,
    then talks to you plainly about what they mean — and it’s only ever as sure as your data lets it be.
  </p>

  <figure
    class="surface surface-lift surface-key rise mt-10 max-w-3xl p-6 sm:p-8"
    aria-label="Rendered example: a coach exchange about last night's sleep"
  >
    <figcaption class="mb-6 flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
      <span class="mono text-[0.66rem] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-ink-faint">
        Conversation &middot; example
      </span>
      <span class="chip chip-accent chip-dot">reads your data first</span>
    </figcaption>

    <div class="turn turn-user">
      <span class="turn-who">You asked</span>
      <p class="turn-body">&ldquo;Did I sleep okay?&rdquo;</p>
    </div>

    <!-- the visible mechanism: it checks your real numbers before answering -->
    <div class="toolcall mt-6" role="group" aria-label="The lookup the coach ran">
      <span class="toolcall-tag">
        <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span> looked up your data &middot; query_metric
      </span>
      <div>
        <span class="k">{'{'} metric:</span> <span class="v">"sleep_hours"</span><span class="k"
          >, window:</span
        > <span class="v">"3d"</span><span class="k">, stat:</span> <span class="v">"series"</span>
        <span class="k">{'}'}</span>
        <span class="ret"
          >&larr; returns: 3 nights &middot; avg <span class="v">6h&nbsp;0m</span> &middot; your usual
          <span class="v">7h&nbsp;30m</span></span
        >
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="turn turn-coach mt-6">
      <span class="turn-who">Healthee</span>
      <div class="turn-body">
        <p>
          Not really. You were short by about an hour and a half, three nights running, and it’s
          starting to show. Tonight, try heading to bed 30 minutes earlier — of everything you could
          change, that’s the one most likely to help.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <hr class="hairline my-6" />

    <p class="mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">
      Every number here came straight from the lookup above — the coach never makes your numbers up.
      And everything it tells you is backed by real research you can read yourself, or it doesn’t say it.
    </p>
  </figure>
</Section>
